# 📝 Basic FastAPI To-Do App (Beginner Friendly)

This is a beginner-level project using **FastAPI** to build a simple **To-Do List REST API** with in-memory data storage (no database required).  
It demonstrates how to set up basic CRUD operations with clean separation of concerns using FastAPI's modular structure.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

todo_notes_api/
├── main.py # Starts the FastAPI app and includes router
├── controller.py # Defines all API endpoints (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
├── models.py # Defines the ToDo data model using Pydantic
├── services.py # Business logic (how data is stored, updated, deleted)
└── README.md # Project documentation (you're here!)

yaml
Copy
Edit

---

## 🧱 Description of Each File

- **`main.py`**  
  Starts the FastAPI app, adds the router, and defines the root `/` endpoint.

- **`controller.py`**  
  Defines the routes like `/todos`, `/todos/{id}` and maps them to logic functions in `services.py`.

- **`models.py`**  
  Defines the structure of a `Todo` item using `Pydantic`, including fields like `id`, `title`, `description`, and `completed`.

- **`services.py`**  
  Contains the actual logic to handle storing, updating, and deleting todos — using an in-memory list (not a database).

